  "details": "**I'm going to touch you:**\n\nImagine if your avatar's hands could physically interact with others and react to contact, like your hand stopping when it touches someone’s head, or two people being able to hold hands and have their arms move together naturally.\n\nImagine giving someone a proper high five, or actually feeling the weight of a hug through motion feedback.\n\n**Wouldn't this take a lot of performance?**\n\nIt doesn't have to! Physbones collisions are already very optimized to the point of easily running on Quest. I can't see why a system like this couldn't be optimized as well.\n\nI'll leave that to the engineers and programmers at VRChat to decide if it's possible or not.\n\n**What if I don't wanna, you dingus? I don't wanna be touched!**\n\nThat's okay! We already have a toggle for that: Avatar interactions. And you can toggle it globally or per person.\n\n*I feel like this could be as big as the Avatar dynamics update was back when it released.*",
